mindmap
  root(("Branch 1: ISTQB CTFL v4.0 test process §1.4"))
    Test planning
      Tasks
        Define test objectives
        Select test approach within constraints
      Work products
        Test plan
        Test schedule
        Risk register
        Entry and exit criteria
    Test monitoring and control
      Tasks
        Check progress against the plan continuously
        Evaluate exit criteria
        Take control actions to meet objectives
      Work products
        Test progress reports
        Documented control directives
        Risk information
    Test analysis: what to test
      Tasks
        Analyse the test basis
        Identify testable features
        Define and prioritise test conditions with risks
        Evaluate test basis for defects and testability
      Work products
        Prioritised test conditions e.g. acceptance criteria
        Defect reports on the test basis
    Test design: how to test
      Tasks
        Elaborate test conditions into test cases
        Identify coverage items
        Define test data requirements
        Design the test environment and tools
      Work products
        Prioritised test cases
        Test charters
        Coverage items
        Test data requirements
        Test environment requirements
    Test implementation
      Tasks
        Create or acquire testware and test data
        Organise test cases into procedures and suites
        Write manual and automated test scripts
        Arrange the test execution schedule
        Build and verify the test environment
      Work products
        Test procedures
        Automated test scripts
        Test suites
        Test data
        Test execution schedule
        Environment items: stubs, drivers, simulators, service virtualisation
    Test execution
      Tasks
        Run tests according to the schedule
        Compare actual and expected results
        Log test results
        Analyse anomalies and report defects
      Work products
        Test logs
        Defect reports
    Test completion
      Tasks
        Raise change requests for unresolved defects
        Archive or hand over reusable testware
        Shut the test environment down to an agreed state
        Collect lessons learned
        Write and communicate the completion report
      Work products
        Test completion report
        Improvement action items
        Documented lessons learned
        Change requests or backlog items
    Cross-cutting
      Activities are iterative or parallel, not strictly sequential §1.4.2
      Process is tailored to context §1.4.2
      Traceability: test basis to testware to results §1.4.4
      Roles: test management role and testing role §1.4.5
      Static testing supports test analysis
